{"name":"Red Contrast","hex":"#b33234","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"contrast","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A difference in lightness, brightness or hue between two colours that makes them more or less distinguishable.\n The degree of this difference.","The degree of this difference."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To set in opposition in order to show the difference or differences between; to counterpoint.","To form a contrast."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contrast"}],"entries":[{"title":"Contrast (vision)","blocks":[{"text":"Contrast is the difference in luminance or color that makes an object distinguishable from a background. Human vision is more sensitive to relative differences than to absolute luminance, so perceived appearance can remain fairly stable despite large changes in illumination."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Contrast_change_photoshop.jpg/330px-Contrast_change_photoshop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contrast_(vision)"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary 